NAME
    feed - resume the game and keep watching it

SYNOPSIS
    feed [-w]

DESCRIPTION
    Resumes gameplay, like 'resume', but leaves a way back to the prompt
    that does not depend on the game window having keyboard focus: press
    Ctrl+C at the TERMINAL and the prompt reopens.

    That watch is a per-frame poll of Console.KeyAvailable, not a blocking
    read - the same non-blocking technique coretop's dashboard uses, spread
    across frames because gameplay has to keep running underneath it. While
    armed, Console.TreatControlCAsInput is set, so Ctrl+C arrives as a
    readable key rather than the process-terminating signal it is
    everywhere else. Entering the prompt by ANY path disarms it, so a plain
    Ctrl+C means 'shut down' again the moment you are back at a prompt.

    -w  Also opens the live picture in a separate window, so gameplay is
        visible without the game window itself being on screen. Refreshed
        at ~30Hz into one reused bitmap. Same accepted read-only race as
        coretop -w: the timer reads core state off the UI thread with no
        synchronization against the emulation thread's own RunFrame.

    In EmuSen.Mistress the word means the same thing but does much less,
    and deliberately so. That frontend's game view is already on screen
    continuously, in the same window, the whole time its console window is
    open - the two are just independent Avalonia windows - so there is no
    separate feed to open. 'feed' there brings the game window to the
    front, for when the console (or something else) is covering it, and
    ignores '-w' the same way that frontend's own 'coretop' does. The
    command exists there for consistency: one word means 'let me see the
    game' everywhere DianaSh runs.

EXAMPLES
    feed
    feed -w
